            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0185" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg125"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your unsatisfied demand for degradation of viceroy Szechuan and delay in British
                    Chengtu investigation makes independent investigation necessary. Can not act
                    peremptorily on reports of commissions to which we are not party. Organize at
                    once an American commission—consul at Tientsin, missionary, and naval officer,
                    with Chinese officer of suitable rank. Should go overland from Tientsin via
                    Tung-kuan and Han-chung in less than thirty days. Notify Chinese Government and
                    ask ample escort. If deposed viceroy’s residence Chengtu likely to obstruct
                    investigation demand that he be ordered elsewhere under complete suspension,
                    pending ulterior demands.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
